.TH LINEAR 1 2000-1月 "profiles_matrix" "profiles_matrix"
.SH NAME
profiles_matrix \- Run the perturbation experiment for a set of genes and collect the profiles into a matrix.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIprofiles_matrix(\fBmodel\fR as <generic> ElasticNet, 
\fBgenes\fR as any, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockdown", 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run the perturbation experiment for a set of genes and collect the profiles into a matrix.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBmodel\fB \fR\- the perturbation engine that is created via \fBelastic_model\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- the target gene ids, one column will be generated for each of them. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR, \fBknockdown\fR (default) or \fBoverexpress\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a matrix of the \fB[gene x condition]\fR mutant means. The genes that can not be found in
 the model are skipped, so the column number equals the number of the matched genes.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
This api is the memory friendly replacement of the \fBmake_exports\fR api for a batch run:
 it does not generate the ten difference analysis tables for every condition.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
linear
.SH FILES
.PP
TRNtoolkit.dll
.PP
